 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "The formula says: R is serial (∀x∃y R(x,y)), antisymmetric, transitive, irreflexive. Pick any a₀; seriality gives a₁ with R(a₀, a₁).",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n0",
     "set": {
      "tone": "accent",
      "fill": "accent"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "n1",
     "set": {
      "tone": "info"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e1",
     "set": {
      "tone": "info"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Seriality again gives a₂ with R(a₁, a₂); transitivity then gives R(a₀, a₂). Continuing, an infinite chain a₀ → a₁ → a₂ → … .",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n2",
     "set": {
      "tone": "info"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e2",
     "set": {
      "tone": "info"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "chain grows: a₀ → a₁ → a₂ → …",
      "tone": "info"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "All aᵢ must be DISTINCT: if aᵢ = aⱼ (i < j), transitivity along the chain gives R(aᵢ, aᵢ), violating irreflexivity; antisymmetry forbids cycles too.",
